Falsifies `capability_table::from_bits_cannot_forge_a_right`.

The defect: the mask dropped from `Rights::from_bits`, `Rights::from_word(bits)` instead of
`Rights::from_word(bits & Rights::ALL.bits())`. `from_bits` takes an attacker-controlled system call
register, so this is the exact shape of a real hole: userspace hands the kernel a u32 and
the kernel believes all 32 bits of it.

Expected to fail: `assert!(Rights::from_bits(raw).is_subset_of(Rights::ALL))`, on any
`raw` with a bit from 5 to 30 set (bit 31 is the marker).

diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -109,7 +109,7 @@
     /// [`bits`](Self::bits), for rights that crossed a boundary in a system call register. Undefined
     /// bits are dropped, so a caller cannot conjure a right that does not exist.
     pub const fn from_bits(bits: u32) -> Rights {
-        Rights::from_word(bits & Rights::ALL.bits())
+        Rights::from_word(bits)
     }
 
     /// Every right either side holds.
